# Every protocol, receipt and result table here publishes a full 64-character
# SHA-256, and MANIFEST.tsv lists one per file. Git's default text=auto stores
# LF and checks out CRLF on Windows, which would change the hash of every
# line-oriented artefact and make MANIFEST.tsv wrong on half the machines that
# clone this. No end-of-line conversion, anywhere.
* -text
